<p>French police have arrested nine people in connection with the killing of Quentin Deranque, a 23-year-old far-right activist who was beaten in Lyon last week. Several outlets link the attack to clashes between far-left and far-right groups, and investigators are treating the case as a homicide inquiry. Le Monde said one of those arrested is a parliamentary aide linked to the radical-left party La France Insoumise, adding a politically sensitive twist to the case.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/_SgFq9ZXGSo8Q1Ftflcrt4BczFfEg0qAQNxbOpijMZY7xYI9dbQgUh9OOjwBQV9e6GO-hfbPiwe8JtAbr1kS5CnVtfoOEh9m4u7gg3QTmE2QgidBVJb-HcqciWfJwTLzeuSECSyJnAPUqJSIrqBNtKrRV3ZIsfw9VWxKbxOP8YNDZHd5QA' alt='Demonstrators gather during a rally in honor of far-right activist Quentin Deranque, in Metz on February 16, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Who the attackers were: The BBC said Deranque was beaten by masked men believed to be far-left militants.</li><li>How the victim is described: The BBC described Deranque as a far-right student, while Al Jazeera called him a security guard.</li><li>Where it happened: The Straits Times said the fatal beating took place outside a conference in Lyon.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>French investigators/police: Authorities detained suspects in a homicide investigation into Deranque’s fatal beating, with reporting linking the case to clashes between far-left and far-right groups. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/18/france-arrests-nine-over-killing-of-far-right-activist-quentin-deranque'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Euronews (political context): The outlet said the killing has fuelled tensions between the far right and hard left as France heads into an election season. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/02/17/four-suspects-arrested-in-killing-of-french-far-right-activist-in-lyon'>Euronews</a>)</li><li>Le Monde (political sensitivity): Le Monde highlighted that the arrests included a parliamentary aide from La France Insou